                  <msItem>
                     <title>Bartholomaeus Anglicus, De proprietatibus rerum</title>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">Two leaves, formerly pastedowns of this book,
                        are now in MS. 36 nos. 4,5. At foot of one these and referring evidently to
                        the book in the binding of which they were is the inscription given above.
                        The book itself has 'constat fratri Iohanni Euesham'.</note>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">For the binding see Oldham, Shrewsbury School
                        Library Bindings, p. 10 ('Pre-Unicorn binder').</note>
                  </msItem>
               </msContents>
